The issue was floating-point imprecision in `invoiceTotal`. The expression `net + net * rate` produced `10.010000000000002` instead of `10.01`.

**Fix:** Added `Math.round(gross * 100) / 100` to round the final result to the nearest cent (half-up).

```js
function invoiceTotal(lines, rate) {
  const net = lines.reduce((sum, l) => sum + lineTotal(l), 0);
  const gross = net + net * rate;
  return Math.round(gross * 100) / 100;
}
```

All 2 tests pass, and `invoiceTotal([{ unitPrice: 9.1, quantity: 1 }], 0.1)` now correctly returns `10.01`.

